  The CLINICAL CONTENT it encodes - the six screening items and the >= 2
  cutoff of the Short Screen for Child Sex Trafficking (SSCST) - is NOT.
  Source: Greenbaum VJ, Dodd M, McCracken C, Pediatric Emergency Care,
  PMID 26599463. That paper is not open access.

  THE REDISTRIBUTION TERMS OF THIS INSTRUMENT HAVE NOT BEEN ESTABLISHED.
  Project Harper has not obtained, and does not claim, any license to it.
  Assume permission is required before clinical or commercial use, and obtain
  your own determination from the rights holder.

  Do not assume a Creative Commons grant: a separate 2022 implementation
  study (Peterson et al., Child Abuse & Neglect) is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, but that
  covers that article, not this instrument, and this encoding does not derive
  from it.

  Whether encoding these items in DMN is a permitted reproduction or a
  derivative work has not been reviewed by counsel. See NOTICE at the
  repository root. Unresolved and under review.
